  "metadata": {
    "job": "Two-sided spacer block",
    "revision": "A",
    "notes": "Two setups, two programs. Bottom-face ops are mirrored about the flip axis, and the two dowel holes are what locates the blank after it is turned over — they sit on the centreline, so the set is unchanged by the mirror. The outline is cut LAST, from the second setup: a part released in setup one cannot be flipped and relocated."
  },
